            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear Colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your 84-year-old male patient, admitted on 16/01/2013 due to an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, clinical examination revealed significant dyspnoea, prolonged expiration, and reduced oxygen saturation. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed hypoxaemia with mild hypercapnia. Chest X-ray excluded pneumonia or pneumothorax. ECG showed no acute cardiac pathology. Blood tests demonstrated elevated inflammatory markers consistent with exacerbation. The patient was treated with supplemental oxygen therapy, nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and intravenous fluids. Vital signs were monitored continuously throughout the stay. The patient responded well to treatment with improving oxygen saturation and reduced dyspnoea. He is discharged on optimised inhaler therapy. Please arrange follow-up and consider pulmonary rehabilitation referral. Do not hesitate to contact me for further information. Yours sincerely, Dr. [Hospital Physician]</div>
               </text>
